<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaysia Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malaysia Agreement was the treaty signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> on 9 July 1963 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a>, Sarawak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, providing for the creation of Malaysia. It set out safeguards for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> states, including control over immigration, and Malaysia was proclaimed on 16 September 1963. Its interpretation remains a political issue in Sabah and Sarawak.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malaysia-agreement.jpg" alt="Malaysia Agreement" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Governments of the UK, Federation of Malaya, North Borneo, Sarawak and Singapore. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agreement_Relating_to_Malaysia_between_UK,_N._Borneo,_Sarawak_and_Singapore.djvu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
